IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpa-dates`
IMPORT `lpa-core`

-- Legal Profession Act 2007 (Qld), Part 3.4 -- costs disclosure, costs agreements, billing and assessment, from the
-- seat of the client.
--
-- SEAT: the client: the person to whom or for whom a law practice provides legal services (s 328(10), s 334), for
-- example a person who retains a law practice to bring a personal injury or compensation claim. "Does Queensland's
-- costs law apply to me? What must my lawyer tell me about costs? Is my costs agreement valid, and what if it is not?
-- Can I cool off? What is the most uplift fee I can be charged? When can my lawyer sue me for the bill, or charge
-- interest? By when must I get my itemised bill? By when must I apply for a costs assessment, and who pays for it?"
-- Every question is asked as the client would ask it, on facts the client can state. Decisions of the law practice's
-- principal, the costs assessor and the court are facts the client answers from what they have been told. The rules
-- are in lpa-core.l4; this module builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same
-- meaning carry the same name in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Act 2007 (Qld) -- the client's questions about legal costs`

-- A placeholder for a date the question's rule does not read.
`a date not used` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000

§§ `Does Queensland's costs law apply to my matter (ss 302-304)`

@export Does Part 3.4 of Queensland's Legal Profession Act 2007 (costs disclosure, costs agreements, billing and costs assessment) apply to my legal matter?
GIVEN `I first instructed my law practice in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice first received your instructions about this matter in Queensland, in person or by post, phone, email or otherwise (s 305)
      `where I first instructed cannot be decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not possible to decide in which jurisdiction you first instructed the law practice
      `my legal work is mainly in Queensland or connected with Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal services are or will be provided wholly or mainly in Queensland, or the matter has a substantial connection with Queensland
      `I accepted a written offer that Part 3.4 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted (in writing or by conduct) a written offer from the law practice that Queensland's Part 3.4 apply to the matter
      `I gave written notice that Part 3.4 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you notified the law practice in writing that you require Queensland's Part 3.4 to apply
      `my notice came more than 28 days after I was told of the right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that notice was given more than 28 days after the law practice told you, under another State's law, of your right to give it (answer no if you gave no notice)
      `my legal work is mainly elsewhere or connected with another jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal services are or will be provided wholly or mainly in another Australian jurisdiction, or the matter has a substantial connection with one
      `I chose the other jurisdiction's costs law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed with the law practice, or notified it in time, under the other jurisdiction's law, that its corresponding costs law is to apply
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
DECIDE `Does Queensland's costs law apply to my matter` IS
    `the Part 3.4 application answer (ss 302-304)` (`Application facts` WITH
        `first instructed in Queensland`                         IS `I first instructed my law practice in Queensland`
        `where first instructed cannot be decided`               IS `where I first instructed cannot be decided`
        `services mainly in Queensland or substantial connection` IS `my legal work is mainly in Queensland or connected with Queensland`
        `accepted a written offer that Part 3.4 apply`           IS `I accepted a written offer that Part 3.4 apply`
        `gave written notice requiring Part 3.4`                 IS `I gave written notice that Part 3.4 apply`
        `the notice was more than 28 days after being told of the right` IS `my notice came more than 28 days after I was told of the right`
        `services mainly elsewhere or substantial connection elsewhere` IS `my legal work is mainly elsewhere or connected with another jurisdiction`
        `chose the other jurisdiction's law under its corresponding law` IS `I chose the other jurisdiction's costs law`)

§§ `What my law practice must tell me about costs (Division 3)`

@export What must my Queensland law practice tell me about its legal costs: nothing, a short (abbreviated) disclosure, or a full written (detailed) disclosure?
GIVEN `my likely legal costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The likely total of the law practice's legal costs in the matter, in Australian dollars, excluding disbursements (outlays such as court fees and medical reports) and excluding GST
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `I will not have to pay the legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will not be required to pay the legal costs and the law practice will not otherwise recover them (for example pro bono work)
      `I had a costs disclosure from this law practice in the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received one or more costs disclosures from this law practice in the previous 12 months
      `I agreed in writing to waive disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed in writing to waive your right to costs disclosure
      `a principal decided further disclosure was not warranted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a principal of the law practice decided that, given the earlier disclosures, further disclosure is not warranted
GIVETH A `Disclosure answer`
DECIDE `What must my law practice tell me about costs` IS
    `the disclosure answer (ss 307A-308, 311)` (`Disclosure facts` WITH
        `the likely legal costs`                                IS `my likely legal costs`
        `the client is a sophisticated client`                  IS `is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`
        `the client will not be required to pay`                IS `I will not have to pay the legal costs`
        `a disclosure was received in the previous 12 months`   IS `I had a costs disclosure from this law practice in the last 12 months`
        `the client agreed in writing to waive disclosure`      IS `I agreed in writing to waive disclosure`
        `a principal decided further disclosure is not warranted` IS `a principal decided further disclosure was not warranted`)

@export Before I sign a costs agreement with an uplift fee (a success fee), must my Queensland law practice tell me in writing its legal costs, the uplift fee or how it is worked out, and why it is warranted?
GIVEN `my costs agreement has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs agreement provides for an uplift fee: additional legal costs (not disbursements) payable if the matter succeeds
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my law practice explain the uplift fee in writing first` IS
    `the law practice must disclose the uplift fee in writing first (s 313)` `my costs agreement has an uplift fee` (`is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`)

@export My Queensland law practice did not tell me something about costs that the Act required: need I pay its legal costs before they are assessed?
GIVEN `my law practice failed to disclose something required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose to you anything Division 3 of Part 3.4 required (for example the basis of its costs, an estimate, your rights, or a substantial change)
      `the failure was only because a law practice it retained did not tell it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure happened solely because a law practice it retained for you (for example a barrister) did not give it the information it needed, and the bill is for the first law practice's own work (answer no if you do not know)
      `my legal costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs have been assessed by a costs assessor under Division 7
GIVETH A `Non-disclosure answer`
DECIDE `Need I pay costs that were not properly disclosed` IS
    `the s 316 answer` `my law practice failed to disclose something required` `the failure was only because a law practice it retained did not tell it` `my legal costs have been assessed`

@export Must my Queensland law practice give me a written report on how my matter is going, or on the legal costs so far, and can it charge me for it?
GIVEN `the report I want` IS A `Report kind` @desc Which report you want: a written report of the progress of the matter, or a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `I am asking a law practice my own law practice retained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking a law practice (for example a barrister) that your own law practice retained for you and that still acts alongside it
GIVETH A `Report answer`
DECIDE `Can I get a written report, and must I pay for it` IS
    `the s 317 answer` `the report I want` (`is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`) `I am asking a law practice my own law practice retained`

§§ `My costs agreement (Division 5)`

@export Is my Queensland costs agreement with my lawyer void under the Legal Profession Act 2007, and if so what can the law practice still recover from me?
GIVEN `my agreement is written or evidenced in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs agreement is in writing or evidenced in writing
      `I accepted a written offer from the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was made by your accepting (in writing or by conduct) a written offer from the law practice
      `the offer said what s 322(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that offer clearly stated that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement, that it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct, and what conduct will count as acceptance (answer yes if there was no such offer)
      `my agreement excludes costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement says the legal costs are not subject to costs assessment
      `my payment depends on winning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paying some or all of the legal costs depends on a successful outcome of the matter ("no win, no fee" or similar)
      `my matter involves criminal or family law proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves criminal proceedings or proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)
      `my agreement says what counts as success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement sets out the circumstances that make up a successful outcome
      `my agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement itself is in writing (not merely evidenced in writing)
      `my agreement is in clear plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is in clear plain language
      `I signed my agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed the agreement
      `my agreement mentions independent legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement states that you were told of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it
      `my agreement's cooling-off period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days of cooling-off (during which you may end the agreement by written notice) the agreement gives you; 0 if none
      `my agreement has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement provides for an uplift fee: additional legal costs (not disbursements) payable if the matter succeeds
      `the uplift fee basis is shown separately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement separately identifies how the uplift fee is calculated (answer yes if there is no uplift fee)
      `my agreement estimates the uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement contains an estimate of the uplift fee, or a range of estimates with an explanation of the major variables (answer yes if there is no uplift fee)
      `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is likely to involve, proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the uplift fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the legal costs before any discount` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs, excluding disbursements, otherwise payable, in Australian dollars, as the law practice would have charged them without any discount
      `my fee is a share of what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount payable to the law practice, or part of it, is calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered in the proceedings
      `my agreement adopts a scale of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that part of the agreement simply adopts an applicable scale of costs (for example a court scale)
      `my agreement gives the law practice my interest in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, instead of your paying the law practice, all or part of your interest in the proceedings is transferred to it
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
GIVETH A `Void answer`
DECIDE `Is my costs agreement void` IS
    `the s 327 answer` `my agreement facts`
    WHERE
        `my agreement facts` MEANS `Costs agreement facts` WITH
            `written or evidenced in writing`                         IS `my agreement is written or evidenced in writing`
            `made by accepting a written offer`                       IS `I accepted a written offer from the law practice`
            `the offer states what s 322(4) requires`                 IS `the offer said what s 322(4) requires`
            `says the costs are not subject to costs assessment`      IS `my agreement excludes costs assessment`
            `payment depends on a successful outcome`                 IS `my payment depends on winning`
            `the matter involves criminal or Family Law Act proceedings` IS `my matter involves criminal or family law proceedings`
            `sets out what counts as a successful outcome`            IS `my agreement says what counts as success`
            `in writing`                                              IS `my agreement is in writing`
            `in clear plain language`                                 IS `my agreement is in clear plain language`
            `signed by the client`                                    IS `I signed my agreement`
            `states the client was told of the right to independent legal advice` IS `my agreement mentions independent legal advice`
            `cooling-off clear business days`                         IS `my agreement's cooling-off period`
            `provides for an uplift fee`                              IS `my agreement has an uplift fee`
            `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified`    IS `the uplift fee basis is shown separately`
            `contains an estimate or range of the uplift fee`         IS `my agreement estimates the uplift fee`
            `the matter is litigious`                                 IS `my matter is litigious`
            `the uplift fee amount`                                   IS `the uplift fee`
            `the undiscounted legal costs otherwise payable`          IS `the legal costs before any discount`
            `the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` IS `my fee is a share of what I recover`
            `the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs`       IS `my agreement adopts a scale of costs`
            `the client's interest in the proceedings passes to the law practice` IS `my agreement gives the law practice my interest in the proceedings`
            `the client is sophisticated`                             IS `is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`

@export Which rules of Division 5 of Queensland's Legal Profession Act 2007 does my costs agreement break (each one makes the agreement void)?
GIVEN `my agreement is written or evidenced in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs agreement is in writing or evidenced in writing
      `I accepted a written offer from the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was made by your accepting (in writing or by conduct) a written offer from the law practice
      `the offer said what s 322(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that offer clearly stated that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement, that it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct, and what conduct will count as acceptance (answer yes if there was no such offer)
      `my agreement excludes costs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement says the legal costs are not subject to costs assessment
      `my payment depends on winning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paying some or all of the legal costs depends on a successful outcome of the matter ("no win, no fee" or similar)
      `my matter involves criminal or family law proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves criminal proceedings or proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)
      `my agreement says what counts as success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement sets out the circumstances that make up a successful outcome
      `my agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement itself is in writing (not merely evidenced in writing)
      `my agreement is in clear plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is in clear plain language
      `I signed my agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed the agreement
      `my agreement mentions independent legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement states that you were told of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it
      `my agreement's cooling-off period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days of cooling-off (during which you may end the agreement by written notice) the agreement gives you; 0 if none
      `my agreement has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement provides for an uplift fee: additional legal costs (not disbursements) payable if the matter succeeds
      `the uplift fee basis is shown separately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement separately identifies how the uplift fee is calculated (answer yes if there is no uplift fee)
      `my agreement estimates the uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement contains an estimate of the uplift fee, or a range of estimates with an explanation of the major variables (answer yes if there is no uplift fee)
      `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is likely to involve, proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the uplift fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the legal costs before any discount` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs, excluding disbursements, otherwise payable, in Australian dollars, as the law practice would have charged them without any discount
      `my fee is a share of what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount payable to the law practice, or part of it, is calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered in the proceedings
      `my agreement adopts a scale of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that part of the agreement simply adopts an applicable scale of costs (for example a court scale)
      `my agreement gives the law practice my interest in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, instead of your paying the law practice, all or part of your interest in the proceedings is transferred to it
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
GIVETH A LIST OF `Contravention`
DECIDE `What rules does my costs agreement break` IS
    `the Division 5 contraventions` `my agreement facts`
    WHERE
        `my agreement facts` MEANS `Costs agreement facts` WITH
            `written or evidenced in writing`                         IS `my agreement is written or evidenced in writing`
            `made by accepting a written offer`                       IS `I accepted a written offer from the law practice`
            `the offer states what s 322(4) requires`                 IS `the offer said what s 322(4) requires`
            `says the costs are not subject to costs assessment`      IS `my agreement excludes costs assessment`
            `payment depends on a successful outcome`                 IS `my payment depends on winning`
            `the matter involves criminal or Family Law Act proceedings` IS `my matter involves criminal or family law proceedings`
            `sets out what counts as a successful outcome`            IS `my agreement says what counts as success`
            `in writing`                                              IS `my agreement is in writing`
            `in clear plain language`                                 IS `my agreement is in clear plain language`
            `signed by the client`                                    IS `I signed my agreement`
            `states the client was told of the right to independent legal advice` IS `my agreement mentions independent legal advice`
            `cooling-off clear business days`                         IS `my agreement's cooling-off period`
            `provides for an uplift fee`                              IS `my agreement has an uplift fee`
            `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified`    IS `the uplift fee basis is shown separately`
            `contains an estimate or range of the uplift fee`         IS `my agreement estimates the uplift fee`
            `the matter is litigious`                                 IS `my matter is litigious`
            `the uplift fee amount`                                   IS `the uplift fee`
            `the undiscounted legal costs otherwise payable`          IS `the legal costs before any discount`
            `the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` IS `my fee is a share of what I recover`
            `the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs`       IS `my agreement adopts a scale of costs`
            `the client's interest in the proceedings passes to the law practice` IS `my agreement gives the law practice my interest in the proceedings`
            `the client is sophisticated`                             IS `is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`

@export In a Queensland "no win, no fee" (conditional) costs agreement for a matter going to court, what is the most uplift fee my lawyer may charge (25% of the undiscounted legal costs)? No answer means s 324(4) sets no cap because the matter is not litigious.
GIVEN `my matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is likely to involve, proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the legal costs before any discount` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs, excluding disbursements, otherwise payable, in Australian dollars, as the law practice would have charged them without any discount
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most uplift fee I can be charged` IS
    `the most uplift fee allowed (s 324(4)-(5))` (`Costs agreement facts` WITH
        -- Only the two fields below are read by the rule; the others are fixed placeholders.
        `written or evidenced in writing`                         IS TRUE
        `made by accepting a written offer`                       IS FALSE
        `the offer states what s 322(4) requires`                 IS TRUE
        `says the costs are not subject to costs assessment`      IS FALSE
        `payment depends on a successful outcome`                 IS TRUE
        `the matter involves criminal or Family Law Act proceedings` IS FALSE
        `sets out what counts as a successful outcome`            IS TRUE
        `in writing`                                              IS TRUE
        `in clear plain language`                                 IS TRUE
        `signed by the client`                                    IS TRUE
        `states the client was told of the right to independent legal advice` IS TRUE
        `cooling-off clear business days`                         IS 5
        `provides for an uplift fee`                              IS TRUE
        `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified`    IS TRUE
        `contains an estimate or range of the uplift fee`         IS TRUE
        `the matter is litigious`                                 IS `my matter is litigious`
        `the uplift fee amount`                                   IS 0
        `the undiscounted legal costs otherwise payable`          IS `the legal costs before any discount`
        `the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` IS FALSE
        `the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs`       IS FALSE
        `the client's interest in the proceedings passes to the law practice` IS FALSE
        `the client is sophisticated`                             IS FALSE)

@export Can I still end my Queensland conditional ("no win, no fee") costs agreement in its cooling-off period, and what can the law practice then charge me?
GIVEN `my payment depends on winning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paying some or all of the legal costs depends on a successful outcome of the matter ("no win, no fee" or similar)
      `my agreement has an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement provides for an uplift fee: additional legal costs (not disbursements) payable if the matter succeeds
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `my agreement's cooling-off period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear business days of cooling-off (during which you may end the agreement by written notice) the agreement gives you; 0 if none
      `business days that ended before my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole business days have ended between the day you made the agreement and the day you give (or will give) written notice ending it, counting neither of those two days
GIVETH A `Cooling-off answer`
DECIDE `Can I still cool off from my conditional costs agreement` IS
    `the s 323 cooling-off answer` (`my payment depends on winning` OR `my agreement has an uplift fee`) (`is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`) `my agreement's cooling-off period` `business days that ended before my notice`

@export Can I ask a Queensland court or tribunal to set aside my costs agreement because it is not fair or reasonable?
GIVEN `I am the client or a paying party to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person to whom or for whom the legal services were provided, or a third party who must pay the law practice and is a party to the costs agreement
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
DECIDE `Can I ask to have my costs agreement set aside` IS
    `the s 328 answer` `I am the client or a paying party to the agreement`

§§ `My bill (ss 321, 329-332, 338)`

@export From what day can my Queensland law practice sue me to recover its legal costs?
GIVEN `I have been given a bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice has given you a bill for the legal costs
      `the day I was given the bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the bill, ISO 8601 (any date if none)
      `my bill was a lump sum bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill states only the total amount and describes the services, rather than itemising the costs in detail
      `I asked for an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the law practice for an itemised bill
      `the day I asked for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked for the itemised bill, ISO 8601 (any date if you did not)
      `I have been given the itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice has given you the itemised bill you asked for
      `the day I was given the itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the itemised bill, ISO 8601 (any date if not yet)
      `my law practice failed to disclose something required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose to you anything Division 3 of Part 3.4 required (for example the basis of its costs, an estimate, your rights, or a substantial change)
      `my legal costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs have been assessed by a costs assessor under Division 7
      `a costs assessment is under way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application for assessment of these costs has been made and the assessment is not yet completed
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
DECIDE `When can my law practice sue me for its costs` IS
    `the earliest recovery proceedings answer (ss 316(2), 329, 332, 338)` (`Recovery facts` WITH
        `bill given`                          IS `I have been given a bill`
        `bill day`                            IS `the day I was given the bill`
        `lump sum bill`                       IS `my bill was a lump sum bill`
        `itemised bill asked for`             IS `I asked for an itemised bill`
        `itemised bill request day`           IS `the day I asked for an itemised bill`
        `itemised bill given`                 IS `I have been given the itemised bill`
        `itemised bill day`                   IS `the day I was given the itemised bill`
        `disclosure failure not yet assessed` IS (`my law practice failed to disclose something required` AND (NOT `my legal costs have been assessed`))
        `costs application pending`           IS `a costs assessment is under way`)

@export I asked my Queensland law practice for an itemised bill after a lump sum bill: by when must it give it to me, and is it late?
GIVEN `my bill was a lump sum bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill states only the total amount and describes the services, rather than itemising the costs in detail
      `the day I asked for an itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked for the itemised bill, ISO 8601
      `I have been given the itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice has given you the itemised bill you asked for
      `the day I was given the itemised bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the itemised bill, ISO 8601 (any date if not yet)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer, usually today, ISO 8601
GIVETH AN `Itemised bill answer`
DECIDE `By when must I get my itemised bill` IS
    `the s 332 answer` `my bill was a lump sum bill` `the day I asked for an itemised bill` `I have been given the itemised bill` `the day I was given the itemised bill` `the day asked about`

@export Can my Queensland law practice charge me interest on my unpaid legal costs?
GIVEN `my costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your costs agreement provides for interest on unpaid legal costs
      `the day I was given the bill` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the bill, ISO 8601
      `my bill states interest and the rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill contains a statement that interest is payable and of the rate of interest
      `the interest rate charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The yearly interest rate the law practice charges, as a percentage (for example 8 for 8%)
      `the maximum rate set by regulation` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum yearly rate of interest on unpaid legal costs prescribed by the Legal Profession Regulation, as a percentage (not deposited with this encoding; check the current regulation)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer, usually today, ISO 8601
GIVETH AN `Interest answer`
DECIDE `Can my law practice charge me interest` IS
    `the s 321 answer` `my costs agreement provides for interest` `the day I was given the bill` `my bill states interest and the rate` `the interest rate charged` `the maximum rate set by regulation` `the day asked about`

§§ `Costs assessment (Division 7)`

@export By when must I apply for an assessment of my Queensland lawyer's legal costs, and can a late application still be dealt with?
GIVEN `I was given a bill or asked to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice gave you a bill or made a request for payment
      `the day of the bill or request` IS A DATE @desc The day the bill was given or the request for payment made, ISO 8601 (any date if neither)
      `I have paid the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the costs (only matters if there was neither a bill nor a request for payment)
      `the day I paid the costs` IS A DATE @desc The day you paid the costs, ISO 8601 (any date if not paid)
      `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a law practice or lawyer, a public company or its subsidiary, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a financial services licensee, a liquidator, administrator or receiver, a professional partnership of more than 20 members, a government Minister, department or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, or a joint venture company or group covered by s 311(1)(c) (answer no if you are an individual)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they will be calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply, or would apply, for the costs assessment, ISO 8601
GIVETH AN `Assessment time answer`
DECIDE `By when must I apply for a costs assessment` IS
    `the s 335 answer` `I was given a bill or asked to pay` `the day of the bill or request` `I have paid the costs` `the day I paid the costs` (`is a sophisticated client (s 300)` `I am a client of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` `my costs were agreed by tender`) `the day I apply`

@export Will the costs assessor assess my Queensland lawyer's disputed costs by the terms of my costs agreement?
GIVEN `my agreement fixes the amount or a rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a provision of the costs agreement states the amount of the disputed costs, or a rate or other means of calculating it (for example hourly rates)
      `my agreement has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or QCAT has set the agreement aside under s 328
      `the assessor is satisfied an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessor is satisfied that the agreement does not comply in a material respect with the disclosure rules, or that Division 5 stops the law practice recovering the costs (for example a void agreement), or the parties have agreed otherwise
GIVETH AN `Agreement assessment answer`
DECIDE `Will the assessor go by my costs agreement` IS
    `the s 340 answer` `my agreement fixes the amount or a rate` `my agreement has been set aside` `the assessor is satisfied an exception applies`

@export Who pays the costs of the assessment of my Queensland lawyer's legal costs?
GIVEN `the legal costs billed` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs put up for assessment, in Australian dollars
      `the legal costs after assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs as fixed by the costs assessor, in Australian dollars
      `the assessor found my law practice did not comply with the disclosure rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessor is satisfied that the law practice failed to comply with Division 3 (costs disclosure)
GIVETH AN `Assessment costs answer`
DECIDE `Who pays for my costs assessment` IS
    `the s 342 answer` `the legal costs billed` `the legal costs after assessment` `the assessor found my law practice did not comply with the disclosure rules`
